  "summary": "The S04 results reviewed at checkpoint 677 enter Chapters 10 and 14. The existing backwards-capacity lemma and one-sided stability proposition cover every power 1+alpha, retaining their old labels and exact alpha=1 conclusions. Under an additional power capacity bound on a fixed integrable density, the full Gauduchon root norm has vanishing tails and a subsequence of clipped continuous solutions converges uniformly to an exact finite-mass equation at the critical coefficient. A logarithmic datum on each fixed Hermitian background has coefficient one, belongs to no higher Lp class and has root tails O((log K)^(-alpha)). Both unrestricted S04 questions and general P07 remain open. The four final inputs, 417 lines, receive two complete manual passes after the last change. The final 1754-page October 9 release and matching homepage are served at the verified public commit.",
